Natas Level 6: Local File Inclusion (LFI)
What You See
A page with an "Input secret:" form field
A link to "View sourcecode"
Step 1: View the Source Code
Clicking "View sourcecode" reveals PHP code similar to:
php
<?php
include "includes/secret.inc";

if(array_key_exists("secret", $_POST)) {
    if($secret == $_POST['secret']) {
        print "Access granted. The password for natas7 is <censored>";
    } else {
        print "Wrong secret";
    }
}
?>
The Vulnerability: include
The line include "includes/secret.inc"; loads a file containing the secret value. But this file is not directly accessible via the browser.
Step 2: Find the Secret
The secret.inc file is stored on the server. You need to read it.
Method: Access the file directly via URL
Since the source tells us the file is at includes/secret.inc, try navigating to:
plain
http://natas6.natas.labs.overthewire.org/includes/secret.inc
This reveals the secret value (e.g., something like FOEIUWGHFEEUHOFUOIW).
Step 3: Submit the Secret
Go back to the main page, enter the secret in the "Input secret:" field, and submit.
Why This Works
The include statement in PHP loads and executes the file server-side
The .inc extension is not protected by the web server — it's served as plain text
Developers often mistakenly assume files in includes/ folders are hidden
