Key Takeaways
Table
Lesson	Explanation
Always view source code	It reveals how the application works
.inc files are dangerous	Web servers often don't block them; they can expose secrets
include/require paths leak info	Knowing the file structure helps find hidden files
Never store secrets in accessible files	Sensitive data should be in protected config files, not web-accessible directories
Related Concept: Local File Inclusion (LFI)
This is a mild form of LFI — where an attacker can read files on the server by manipulating file paths. In more severe cases, you can use ../ (directory traversal) to read system files like /etc/passwd
